From 2d583c1cca0f7289f46006ec619aac6606b74c3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:00:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/dma, hw/display, hw/misc: SAM D5x DMAC, ST7789, WS2812;
 the PyKit Ruler

DMAC U2503 (mchp-dmac): descriptors and write-back in SRAM, burst/block/
transaction triggers paced by peripheral flags (SERCOM DRE/RXC, from the
generated trigger table now in MchpDeviceInfo), software triggers, block
actions, five IRQ lines; a started transfer runs at the next status read
or 20 us later, never inside the starting write (firmware clears
CHINTFLAG right after ENABLE). CircuitPython SPI writes and reads by DMA
work.

ST7789V TFT driver (st7789) with the pp_panel picture, MADCTL, 16/18-bit
pixels, inversion and a backlight input. WS2812 chain (ws2812) decoding
the data line by high time over bit period, with "pixels" and "gen".

curiosity-circuitpython gains the PyKit Ruler: the 1.14" 135x240 IPS
display on SERCOM0 (CS PA07, D/C PB14, active-low backlight PA06), five
NeoPixels on PB22, the I2C pull-ups on PB30/PB31. The USB host polls
every 125 us. qtests for the DMAC and the NeoPixels.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
